From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 02:17:39 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: xrx500-cbm: report the driver's own counters through
 ethtool

The driver keeps the accounting the hardware does not: the transmit path
has no completion interrupt, so nothing but the driver knows how many
segments went to the hardware and came back, or how often the queue was
stopped for an exhausted pool and released again; and the receive path
sees descriptors the frame counters never hear about, because a
descriptor rejected as malformed is not a frame.

All of it was reachable only by writing to a module parameter and
reading the log. Report it as a statistics string set instead, so the
ordinary tools can sample it, difference it and script against it, and
drop the two parameters: every counter they printed is now a string set
entry that any tool can read without a writable parameter and without
the log, and the configuration the receive report printed beside its
counters - the ring length, the buffer size and the byte offset - is
already logged where it is decided, when the ring is built.

The per-source-port block is what makes a misdirected delivery visible
on a conduit that serves a switch: the switch header names the port a
frame came in on, and every frame should be counted under the port whose
user device it ends up on.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

